  "question": {
    "text": "The tops of two poles of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> are connected by a wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>30</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><em>.</em> If the wire makes an angle <math><mi>α</mi></math>&nbsp;with the horizontal, then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mi>α</mi></math> is equal to (take,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0.35",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/3a65a34c-810c-493f-9943-80a5cb61ac26.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.2in;height:1.68681in\" /></p><p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></math> and <math><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math> be the two poles.<br /><math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></math> is the length of the wire.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;is the horizontal through <math><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>30</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>35</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
